*sudden screeching* WOAH, WHAT THE FUCKIN' DELAYED-REACTION, DOOR.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:48.000
I never expected the delayed-reaction door.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:51.980
Oh, man! *giggles* Oh, okay. Alright. Sorry.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.020
Physics-based delayed-reaction door.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.200
Alright, Imma go- wait, did I miss something over here?

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:57.880
Oh, I did.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:11:59.840
No, wait, I saved, that was it.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.780
Oh, God.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:02.680
i don't want to go down there.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:03.320
Okay!

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:08.400
*click* Hello? Alright, which one of these doors is gonna- *doll emerges loudly* -crumble on me?

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:09.880
Nope, nope, ain't gonna hit me. *gunshots*

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:11.980
Missed me. And now you're dead.

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:14.760
*click* Find the key to open the office room.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.940
Okay, so that's the office. I got some extra ammo.

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.940
And I'm doing pretty good on able to kill these things.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:26.060
It's been a while since I've played a horror game that actually involved combat, becau- *girl screeching*

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.700
Bah, fuck you. *gunshots* Woah, what the fuck.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:37.360
*gunshot* Because usually- not always, but usually- combat removes a little bit of the scare to it because you're, you're, you're less- you know, you're less-

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:45.340
-threatened when you're just you and yourself with a GUN, instead of just using yourself with shit in your pants.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:52.880
You know? It's usually like a trade-off, but, in this one, it seems to be working pretty well because the original Cry of Fear was all about weapons and killing the things,

00:12:52.880 --> 00:13:01.720
-but it was just so interesting in the diverse environment that you were in, that it created this, uh, unique world that was just fun to go through and terrifying at the same time.

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:05.800
And always with the new monsters coming around every corner, it really made it diverse.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:06.500
Woman: "Here it is."

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:09.840
Mark: Okay. The truth!

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:10.940
The truth!

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:14.100
Wilhelm: "Hi, I am Wilhelm Gefharweitz."

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:18.100
"If you are listening to this, perhaps I am no longer alive."

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.600
Mark: That wasn't him up there either.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:22.700
Wilhelm: "I have found the truth about the mystery of this museum."

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:28.500
"In the past, this place was a nursery that looked after the children-"

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:31.580
"-who were affected by World War II."

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.440
Mark: Noble.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.260
Wilhelm: "After that, this place was burned."

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.340
"And I found out that it was caused by the denomic rituals."

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:41.380
Woman: "What?"

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:43.340
Mark: Yeah, what?

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:47.680
Wilhelm: "In the rituals, the host must kill the victim as a sacrifice to Satan."

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.880
Mark, quietly:  the Satan..?

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:51.360
[quick note, the voices speak in not-my-first-language English voices, so Mark was kinda pointing to that with the previous comment]

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:58.360
"They believe that if they offer a lot of people at the same time at the same place in the most torturous of ways, they will gain incredible power."

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:06.100
"It leads the host to be successful in their life and nothing can stop them."

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:10.040
"They will be more powerful than any human being.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:18.820
"Now, I guess you know what I mean. It is regretful to hear that everyone was killed."

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.840
"The fire burned everything into ashes."

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:29.380
"Then years and years after, this doll museum had been constructed over the place."

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:29.980
Mark: Why?

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:31.440
Woman: "What the heck is it?"

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:32.920
Mark: What the heck indeed!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:33.940
Indeed!

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:37.980
Wilhelm: "I think you will wonder what's happening with the guy who was being the host."

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.560
"No doubt with a Satan curse."

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:41.820
Mark: The Satin curse.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:45.720
Wilhelm: "He was successful in the life that he wanted for a short period of time."

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:50.440
"His life was like a dream for fifteen years."

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:55.940
"Unfortunately, he found out that it was not as good as it should have been."

00:14:56.400 --> 00:15:00.320
"Later, he had found out that the ritual was not complete."

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:03.140
"Someone was gone from the ritual."

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:05.880
"That irritated him so much."

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:10.120
"But finally, he know who was the final one."

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:11.280
Mark: Is it me?

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:12.180
Is it me?

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:12.680
Wilhelm: "Yes."

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:13.740
Mark: Me?

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:17.740
Wilhelm: [Mark: Yay!] "The final one- [Mark: Haha.] -is you, Miss Walterson!"

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:18.760
Mark: That doesn't make any sense.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:19.260
*strange noise*

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:21.300
Hey, ow, my face.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:22.680
Why you do that?

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.260
I knew he wasn't dead!

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:28.820
Oh, save game?

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.000
Sav- Save game?

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:32.380
Okay.

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:41.820
Wilhelm: "Ahh! The big mistake from fifteen years ago will end. [Mark: We could not.] My demonic rituals and everything will be complete!"

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:42.380
Mark: How about we don't?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:45.460
Wilhelm: "All suffering will be gone!"

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.440
Mark: No, thank you.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.400
Wilhelm: Hahaha!

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:49.160
*Walterson groans in pain*

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:53.380
Wilhelm: "Oh, I'm sorry, Miss Walterson. Did I wake you up?"

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:54.100
Mark: Huh.

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:58.540
Wilhelm: "Don't you know that I have been looking for you for a long, long time?"

00:15:58.580 --> 00:15:59.780
Mark: No, I didn't know.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:03.080
Wilhelm: "But at last, I found YOU."

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:03.580
Mark: Okay.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:06.700
Wilhelm: "I didn't expect that you would become a detective."

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:10.220
"It looks like you want to know about your past."

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:13.780
"Yes, I will grant you your wish."

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:14.360
Mark: Okay.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.240
Wilhelm: "I would like to introduce someone to you, too."

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:17.560
Mark: Oh, boy!

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:21.500
Wilhelm: That someone is Satan, who whispered to me."

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.200
Mark: Okay.

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:25.120
Wilhelm: "I really like its soul."

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:25.980
Mark: Oh.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:30.300
Wilhelm: "Yes. Satan said that your mom was so delicious."

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.240
Mark: Ah, that's a weird thing to say.

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:32.900
*Wilhelm laughs*

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:34.360
Mark: In multiple ways.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:37.680
Wilhelm: "Now, it's time to see your mother."

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.000
Mark: Oh. Lovely!

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:46.060
Family reunions are always good. *Wilhelm laughs*

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.440
HAHAHAHA- oh, hi.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:53.040
Oh, oh, oh my God, okay. Well, this was unexpe- oh my God.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:54.240
Are you kidding me?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.900
This is awesome! *giggle*

00:16:55.920 --> 00:16:56.960
This is awesom-

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:58.440
AH Hey, hey, stop that.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.960
Hey- Stop it.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.780
Stop it

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:01.980
You're f-super freaky

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.400
And I- Ooh heart

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:04.980
Oh- ayeee

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:05.820
There we go.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.720
I found your weakness.

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:08.800
It's your- your-

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.780
Conspicuously open heart.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:14.100
And stabbing mechanisms won't work because I'm all the way back here. :(

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:15.760
*pew pew pew*

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.240
Who knew that I could have guns in Hell?!

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:20.020
oh boi

00:17:20.480 --> 00:17:21.320
incoming.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.200
ooh boi- ow my face

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.580
ow my face

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.740
*pew pew pew pew pewdiepie pew pew*

00:17:27.180 --> 00:17:28.360
woooooooah

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.860
YEAH!! I KILLED SATAN!!

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:33.840
I killed him! I killed him dead!

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:35.520
He's dead now! (jeez mark)

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:37.480
I am the winner! (yeah okay)

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.200
of Hell? I guess I get that now?

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.900
That's nice I-I suppose

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:42.640
Oh shit.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.200
Ah fuck.

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.060
You thought they would've learned their lesson the first time.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:50.980
..when they built the museum of horrifying dolls on top of the

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.080
flaming wreckage of a

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:55.040
an abandoned orphanage

00:17:55.780 --> 00:17:57.780
filled with DEAD CHILDREN because

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:59.640
someone probably would've known about it.

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:03.000
Also, how did she survive??

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.260
How did she escape??

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:06.980
She tuck and rolled as a toddler out the window

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.500
but somehow didn't learn those skills now?

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:11.420
As a toddler:

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.220
*touches forehead* "OH GOD DEMONIC FIRE!"

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:14.820
you BUST outta the window

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.000
roll a few feet

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.560
hit your head, lose your memory,

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:20.680
then become a detective and lose all those survival skills.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.940
except when you get a gun and shoot Satan in the heart.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.340
But either way, that was The Final One.

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.440
The name makes sense now, I totally get it.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.500
There were some

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.020
hiccups in this

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:33.660
but it's outweighed by the fact that I

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.760
actually really enjoyed the gameplay.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.080
Obviously, the narration wasn't perfect because

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.100
they didn't speak English as their first language,

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:40.680
um

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.020
but this was good.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.900
It had good flow to it,

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:46.980
and I actually liked the combat.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:50.280
I haven't said that about a horror game, in a long time,

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.600
and I think it's because it's reminiscent of Cry of Fear.

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.860
There were a diverse number of enemies,

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.100
for how short the game was,

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.280
There were like three different enemy types.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.580
Four if you include the first doll that came after you,

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:01.160
but

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.540
i-it's just really interesting to see how

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:05.460
combat /can/ work,

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.400
if you have a diverse enough

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.820
environment and enemy type

00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:12.260
that keeps things interesting.

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:13.660
But either way, I'll leave it at that.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:15.900
Lemme know what you guys thought of it down in the comments below.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.300
I am going to rest my tounge.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.380
I don't know how I'm gonna do that,

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.280
and that just sounds weird when I say it out loud,

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:23.940
But I'm gonna...do just that but

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:26.060
Thank you everybody so much for watching,

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.220
And as always,

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:28.540
I will see you-

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:29.980
in the next video.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:31.560
Buh bye!

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:41.640
*Outro Music*

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.200
Thanks for watching! :D

